IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g6-nouns`
IMPORT `g6-schedule-three`

-- g6-tests-schedule-three.l4: tests of s.41 and the Third Schedule.
-- Every expected value below was read off the gazette page (Sefer HaChukim 3349, p. 205, the Third
-- Schedule) and s.41 (p. 193) BEFORE any run of the module, not off the module:
--   item  individual  corporation
--   (1)     20,000        -
--   (2)     10,000        -
--   (3)      5,000     10,000
--   (4)     20,000        -
--   (5)     20,000     40,000
--   (6)     10,000     20,000
--   (7)      3,000      6,000
-- (a dash is shown as - here; in the Law it is a long dash).
-- s.41(b): an order's column B amount may not exceed 40,000, or 80,000 if the violator is a corporation.
-- s.63(b), IP16: a violation before Chapter 6 commenced is not sanctionable.

§ `Tests of s 41 and the Third Schedule`

§§ `Fixtures`

`an individual violator` MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-IND", `kind of person` IS `an individual`
`a corporate violator`   MEANS Person WITH `reference for the person` IS "P-CORP", `kind of person` IS `a corporation`

`violation (1)` MEANS `work with no licence at all`
`violation (2)` MEANS `work without a licence of the kind appropriate to the system`
`violation (3)` MEANS `advertising as licensed without the licence or the kind`
`violation (4)` MEANS `installation without the tightness test of the piping`
`violation (5)` MEANS `engaging a person who had no licence at all`
`violation (6)` MEANS `engaging a person without a licence of the appropriate kind`
`violation (7)` MEANS `failing to give a document an inspector demanded`

GIVEN who IS A Person
      item IS A `Listed violation`
GIVETH A Violation
`a violation by` who `of` item MEANS
    Violation WITH `the violator` IS who
                 , `the listed violation` IS item
                 , `reference for the act` IS "act-1"
                 , `date of the act` IS YMD 2027 3 1

§§ `Third Schedule column B, cell by cell (p. 205)`

#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (1)` EQUALS JUST 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (2)` EQUALS JUST 10_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (3)` EQUALS JUST 5_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (4)` EQUALS JUST 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (5)` EQUALS JUST 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (6)` EQUALS JUST 10_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `an individual` `and` `violation (7)` EQUALS JUST 3_000

#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (1)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (2)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (3)` EQUALS JUST 10_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (4)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (5)` EQUALS JUST 40_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (6)` EQUALS JUST 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — column B sets, for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (7)` EQUALS JUST 6_000

§§ `The amount the Third Schedule fixes: numbers where the Law prints one, a named refusal at a dash (T14)`

#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (1)` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (2)` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (3)` EQUALS 5_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (4)` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (5)` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (6)` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `an individual` `and` `violation (7)` EQUALS 3_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (3)` EQUALS 10_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (5)` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (6)` EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (7)` EQUALS 6_000

#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (1)` BECAUSE "s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (2)` BECAUSE "s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out"
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for` `a corporation` `and` `violation (4)` BECAUSE "s 41(a) — column B sets no amount here, and the Law does not say whether a dash means that no sanction may be imposed or that a figure was left out"

-- The same through the Violation record, which carries the violator's kind.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) EQUALS 20_000
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)`) EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — the amount the Third Schedule fixes for the violation` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (1)`)

§§ `The Third Schedule as a table: seven rows, the item numbers in order, the provision each contravenes`

#ASSERT count `the Third Schedule` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT map (GIVEN row YIELD row's `the item number`) `the Third Schedule` EQUALS LIST 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7
#ASSERT (`Third Schedule — the row for` `violation (4)`)'s `the item number` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT (`Third Schedule — the row for` `violation (7)`)'s `the item number` EQUALS 7
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (1)` EQUALS `contravenes section 3(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (2)` EQUALS `contravenes section 3(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (3)` EQUALS `contravenes section 4`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (4)` EQUALS `contravenes section 13`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (5)` EQUALS `contravenes section 18(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (6)` EQUALS `contravenes section 18(a)`
#ASSERT `Third Schedule — the provision contravened by` `violation (7)` EQUALS `contravenes section 31(2)`

§§ `s 41(a): the Commissioner may impose a sanction (inputs: Chapter 6 in force, the authorisation, the violation)`

-- Chapter 6 in force, the officer authorised, an individual, item (1): yes.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) TRUE TRUE
-- Chapter 6 not yet in force on the day of the act: no, for an individual ...
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) FALSE TRUE
-- ... and no for a corporation at a dash too: the Law has already answered, the dash is not reached.
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (1)`) FALSE TRUE
-- The officer is not one the Minister authorised for Chapter 6: no.
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (5)`) TRUE FALSE
-- Chapter 6 in force and the officer authorised, a corporation, item (3) (a figure is printed): yes.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (3)`) TRUE TRUE
-- ... and at item (5) and (6) and (7).
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (5)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (6)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (7)`) TRUE TRUE
-- A corporation at a dash (items (1), (2), (4)), everything else holding: the Law does not answer.
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (1)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (2)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT REFUSED `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (4)`) TRUE TRUE
-- An individual at items (1), (2), (4): the Law prints a figure: yes.
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (2)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(a) — a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (4)`) TRUE TRUE

-- The power as a deontic: a MAY the Commissioner exercises, or leaves unexercised (FULFILLED either way).
#TRACE `s 41(a) — the Commissioner may impose the financial sanction for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `impose the financial sanction the Third Schedule fixes for the breach` `the Commissioner` AT 10
#TRACE `s 41(a) — the Commissioner may impose the financial sanction for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 400)
#TRACE `s 41(a) — the Commissioner may impose the financial sanction for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 5)

§§ `s 41(b): the cap on what an order may set (40,000; 80,000 for a corporation)`

#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `an individual` EQUALS 40_000
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the cap on a column B amount for` `a corporation` EQUALS 80_000
-- "shall not exceed": the cap itself is allowed, one shekel above is not.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `an individual` `holding` (JUST 40_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `an individual` `holding` (JUST 40_001)
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `a corporation` `holding` (JUST 80_000)
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `a corporation` `holding` (JUST 80_001)
-- An individual's cap is not a corporation's: 40,001 is over the first and under the second.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `a corporation` `holding` (JUST 40_001)
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `an individual` `holding` (JUST 79_999)
-- A dash sets no amount, so it exceeds no cap.
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the column B cell is within the cap for` `a corporation` `holding` NOTHING

`an order's row with the individual cell over the cap` MEANS `Third Schedule row` OF 8, `work with no licence at all`, `contravenes section 3(a)`, JUST 40_001, NOTHING
`an order's row with the corporation cell over the cap` MEANS `Third Schedule row` OF 8, `work with no licence at all`, `contravenes section 3(a)`, JUST 5_000, JUST 80_001
`an order's row at both caps` MEANS `Third Schedule row` OF 8, `work with no licence at all`, `contravenes section 3(a)`, JUST 40_000, JUST 80_000

-- (Positional OF follows the DECLARE order of `Third Schedule row`: item, violation, provision, individual, corporation.)
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — both column B cells of the row are within the cap` `an order's row at both caps`
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — both column B cells of the row are within the cap` `an order's row with the individual cell over the cap`
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — both column B cells of the row are within the cap` `an order's row with the corporation cell over the cap`
-- The Schedule as enacted respects its own cap (the highest cells are 20,000 and 40,000).
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — every row is within the cap` `the Third Schedule`
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — every row is within the cap` (LIST `Third Schedule item (1)`, `an order's row with the corporation cell over the cap`)

§§ `s 41(b): the Minister's power needs the Minister of Justice's consent and the Committee's approval, and the cap`

#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` `the Third Schedule` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (LIST `an order's row at both caps`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` `the Third Schedule` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` `the Third Schedule` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by an order that sets` (LIST `an order's row with the individual cell over the cap`) TRUE TRUE
#TRACE `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by order` `the Third Schedule` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Minister` DOES `change the Third Schedule by order` `the Minister` AT 1
#TRACE `s 41(b) — the Minister may change the Third Schedule by order` `the Third Schedule` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 1)

§§ `The alternative reading of a dash (F-DASH): no sanction may be imposed where column B prints a dash`

-- Callable: it answers FALSE for a corporation at items (1), (2) and (4), where the reading taken refuses; elsewhere it agrees.
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (1)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (2)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (4)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `a corporate violator` `of` `violation (3)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT     `s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `s 41(a) — reading a dash as no sanction, a financial sanction may be imposed for` (`a violation by` `an individual violator` `of` `violation (1)`) FALSE TRUE
